{"w":2400,"h":3106,"lines":[{"t":"Sample answers for Writing tasks","x":0.56578947062329288,"w":0.29511278788248696,"c":1,"y":0.082743077764121931,"h":0.020605280103026424},{"c":1,"t":"TEST 1, WRITING TASK 2","y":0.12883832703724551,"x":0.088160153977030448,"w":0.33115971883138018,"h":0.023777509150164189},{"w":0.18609022776285811,"x":0.088345863468195021,"y":0.16709594321373911,"t":"SAMPLE ANSWER","h":0.014590103090461937,"c":1},{"x":0.086466156512142525,"t":"This is an answer written by a candidate who achieved a Band 6.5 score. Here is the","c":1,"y":0.20347714095775549,"w":0.73872182210286463,"h":0.017453091726407521},{"y":0.22086284593690919,"w":0.19172931671142579,"h":0.014602269960539815,"x":0.086466168336016405,"c":1,"t":"examiner's comment:"},{"c":1,"y":0.25578654015063096,"w":0.71438959757486986,"x":0.12964104747463503,"t":"The candidate deals with both parts of the prompt and addresses some social and","h":0.019639675339344409},{"t":"practical problems that might be experienced in a foreign language environment.","c":1,"w":0.69938542683919269,"h":0.019191739487018578,"y":0.27366287723496185,"x":0.12963899683973693},{"y":0.29355531894339471,"h":0.016997672017742826,"w":0.69370442708333335,"c":1,"x":0.12776420898106192,"t":"Ideas are supported by examples, though there is room for turther development"},{"h":0.015988371407532842,"t":"here. Organisation is logical and there is clear progression throughout the","c":1,"x":0.12969924560051255,"w":0.63909774780273443,"y":0.30959302339870454},{"x":0.12772169970441127,"y":0.32639332574541546,"w":0.65429931640624994,"h":0.021886956975756267,"t":"response. Cohesive devices are used appropriately [Another problem | For","c":1},{"t":"example | Therefore | That means ... | The second ... problem | To summarize].","y":0.34364497136999494,"w":0.69011306762695312,"x":0.12958184603771827,"h":0.021781417836854278,"c":1},{"t":"There is a sufficient range of vocabulary to allow some flexibility and precision and","y":0.36300874534351368,"x":0.12962427164268642,"c":1,"h":0.019584620144777132,"w":0.71254928588867184},{"t":"to demonstrate awareness of style and collocation [language barrier | linked to |","h":0.021285723350313646,"c":1,"y":0.38037422719055269,"x":0.12769670679585773,"w":0.69198689778645828},{"c":1,"x":0.12773222110273233,"t":"influence the behaviour | offend | misunderstanding | misconceptions]. There is a","y":0.39888422106612831,"w":0.69941721598307294,"h":0.02007580540369025},{"h":0.018426509496095589,"w":0.69748870849609368,"y":0.41696735223491865,"c":1,"t":"mix of simple and complex sentence forms including subordinate clauses [which","x":0.12776542518798256},{"y":0.43593045737547342,"c":1,"h":0.017707662588538176,"t":"means that | a person who], modal verbs [should | might | would] and gerunds","w":0.67481201171874994,"x":0.12781955792227839},{"t":"[finding a job]. Grammatical control is generally good as is the use of punctuation,","y":0.45181270983528632,"w":0.71066884358723958,"c":1,"x":0.12774867441929746,"h":0.020598770185815685},{"x":0.12772819483435147,"c":1,"y":0.46976585134250792,"w":0.57540674845377604,"h":0.019644407479899706,"t":"although the first sentence in the second paragraph is incomplete."},{"y":0.49737014055105377,"x":0.08451262536171375,"w":0.73697575887044264,"h":0.02159319826655437,"c":1,"t":"It is clear that living in a foreign country has its own benefits and drawbacks to consider. I agre"},{"c":1,"w":0.76879699707031257,"t":"with this statement, however I think that anybody coming in another country should respect national","h":0.020383466387746907,"x":0.084586463674435119,"y":0.51889534898891765},{"h":0.020348836895119127,"c":1,"y":0.53924418619498082,"t":"culture. In this essay, I would like to outline the social and practical problems.","w":0.60150375366210929,"x":0.084586468791476216},{"w":0.74833109537760423,"x":0.082576822150810095,"c":1,"h":0.023255313202709904,"t":"The social problems would be language barrier, which means that a person coming from another","y":0.56629360230865822},{"c":1,"h":0.023240801141251266,"x":0.082613782697560229,"y":0.58694518459758516,"t":"country might not be able to speak and understand the language which might be a problem as far","w":0.7595785013834635},{"x":0.084586478162942833,"y":0.60901162791331853,"h":0.018895348808647183,"t":"a person who is living in a country, and a person who came in the country. Another problem is","c":1,"w":0.73308268229166662},{"w":0.74083643595377602,"c":1,"h":0.023167263210318811,"y":0.62770626857254763,"x":0.08257547820540348,"t":"linked to the language barrier, but it might influence the behaviour of others. An individual who"},{"t":"come into the country might offend others with their behaviour or language. For example; some","y":0.64650085693520409,"w":0.73908498128255207,"x":0.082535962148410719,"h":0.026535637211354435,"c":1},{"t":"cultures like English people prefer to be very polite and say things differently from other cultures.","c":1,"x":0.082706775615037226,"y":0.66860465084271503,"h":0.021802326209761635,"w":0.76127817789713537},{"c":1,"x":0.082608199875152569,"t":"Therefore a person who doesn't know how to behave in a particular culture might offend others","y":0.68977636602873338,"w":0.7370170593261719,"h":0.022853260568396427},{"c":1,"y":0.70997381222653067,"t":"around him.","x":0.08251250519180843,"w":0.10021547953287761,"h":0.017718232223009722},{"y":0.73982558154783651,"w":0.75751881917317709,"t":"The practical problems would be misunderstanding of culture. That means that a person who visits","x":0.082706755655560946,"h":0.020348836895119238,"c":1},{"h":0.021270464561251146,"t":"other countries does not understand other culture and he behaves as he wants to.","y":0.75788893818986891,"x":0.082572710623667833,"w":0.63754425048828134,"c":1},{"w":0.76904296875,"c":1,"y":0.78651461970517511,"h":0.023849269918526539,"t":"The second practical problem is finding a job. An individual who works in foreign country might not","x":0.080700349731996635},{"x":0.080768845276922144,"y":0.80786035836097236,"w":0.7407186381022135,"t":"be appropriate for people who he serves. For example if an individual works in a restaurant, the","h":0.020714213904916901,"c":1},{"c":1,"w":0.75939849853515629,"h":0.018895348808647183,"t":"people who live in a country and they were born in that country might not respect and not like the","x":0.082706765560400963,"y":0.82994186047367147},{"w":0.7446392822265625,"x":0.082557101617102363,"t":"behaviour of a person who works in a restaurant, it might be because, the cultures are different.","y":0.84835126123689364,"h":0.023888306086553124,"c":1},{"t":"To summarize, it can be said that there are a lot of misconceptions which people have when they","h":0.02266116243597005,"w":0.74460657755533854,"x":0.080707247138991633,"y":0.87709142182650268,"c":1},{"h":0.019055391693606483,"w":0.72368423461914066,"c":1,"y":0.89954925944931274,"t":"come in a foreign country, and in my opinion and from my personal experience people should","x":0.080827055456479405},{"x":0.080712148415171797,"t":"educate themselves in order to know how to behave in different situations with different cultures.","w":0.7502841695149739,"y":0.91740667793410369,"h":0.021602284271181271,"c":1},{"y":0.9593023256000448,"x":0.81578947296236137,"w":0.033834587732950783,"c":1,"h":0.013081395234588844,"t":"127"}]}